ngle run","caption":"Little @ about 5 ft","poi_name":"boogie water","subject":"Eric Gardner","author":"Brad Beggs","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/878784","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/878784"}},{"id":"878785","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879217","description":"First large rapid on Little at about 5 ft. Notice wood pile, it was helpful at catching our swimmer's boat that day. About 30 degrees, cold water- sounds like a good day to swim, eh? ","caption":"upstream @ 5ft","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Eric Gardner","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/878785","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/878785"}},{"id":"878786","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879218","description":"Little at about 5 ft on nice COLD december day- greta flow! ","caption":"Randy on Little","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Eric Gardner","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/878786","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/878786"}},{"id":"878787","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879219","description":"Little at about 4.5 ft on COLD december day","caption":"Eric boof @ 4.5 ft","poi_name":"","subject":"Eric Gardner","author":"Brad Beggs","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/878787","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/878787"}},{"id":"878788","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879220","description":"Brad on river left boof on Littel at about 4.5 ft. ","caption":"Brad on river left boof","poi_name":"","subject":"Brad Beggs","author":"Eric Gardner","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/878788","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/878788"}},{"id":"882138","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"884821","description":"","caption":"Gorge Boof","poi_name":"Little River Gorge","subject":"Daniel","author":"B.Dixon","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/882138","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/882138"}},{"id":"15134","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8057","description":"","caption":"The Little","poi_name":"","subject":"Mark Thompson","author":"Brian Carver","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/15134","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/15134"}},{"id":"coy5g2YPDj3L63U0ieCbm","ext":"jpg","post_id":"sGZiQn52qq8nu3ZKb1NwH","description":"","caption":"Fossil Rapid","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Zach Schiada","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-08-10T12:47:12.000Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T12:47:12.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/coy5g2YPDj3L63U0ieCbm","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/coy5g2YPDj3L63U0ieCbm"}},{"id":"vSucGmzoQ08ilfLnA2oOF","ext":"jpg","post_id":"3j3mu6lIh4HpccYvtBhJN","description":"South Fork Little River above S Lowell Rd.","caption":"Russell Mill Ledge","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Zach Schiada","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-12-28T12:48:51.000Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T12:48:51.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/vSucGmzoQ08ilfLnA2oOF","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/vSucGmzoQ08ilfLnA2oOF"}},{"id":"q36XzweQz5elWUpFLGiBW","ext":"jpg","post_id":"sGZiQn52qq8nu3ZKb1NwH","description":"This is on the South Fork Little River about a tenth of a mile above S Lowell Rd. It was the site of a 9 ft dam (Benner & McCloud) and used to be the location of Russell Mill. I have not been able to find information about when the dam was destroyed, but what is left is a nice 6 ft river wide ledge.","caption":"Russell Mill Ledge","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Zach Schiada","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-08-10T12:47:12.000Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T12:47:12.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/q36XzweQz5elWUpFLGiBW","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/q36XzweQz5elWUpFLGiBW"}},{"id":"HcShwxTfpBQW8PwgK7eTC","ext":"jpg","post_id":"3j3mu6lIh4HpccYvtBhJN","description":"","caption":"South Fork Little","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Zach Schiada","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-12-28T12:48:51.000Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T12:48:51.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/HcShwxTfpBQW8PwgK7eTC","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/HcShwxTfpBQW8PwgK7eTC"}}],"detail":{"id":"1094","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"Says robert martin 2001-02-07 17:06:24\n\nHere are some notes from Russ Condrey, a paddling legend. At 3.2' USGS it's like the Nantahala+, at 4.8' it's excellent, at 7.2' it's huge (Upper Gauley), at 10.4' it's scary.\n\nOther notes from Russ: 2.0 is painfully low. 3.0' to 5.0' is a good level. 5.0' it gets pushy.\n\nIf you look on a map there are two possible put-ins above Johnson's Mill Road, one is on South Lowell rd. Before Hurricane Fran this was a good warm-up before the Micro-gorge below Johnson's Mill Rd. They have developed this area heavily, so you will be paddling through people's back yards. Due to the Eno River Society, areas of this unique river are being saved from developement and turned into a park. This river also harbors the Roanoke Bass, a spieces of fish that has become threatened in the last few years. They are locally know as 'red eyes'. They thrive in swift moving waters. What better fish could represent whitewater boaters.\n\nrobert martin 2000-10-16 12:48:27\n\nThe most challenging 1/4 mile of whitewater on the Piedmont of North Carolina, no joke. It's like being on an Appalachian Creek! At high water it's class V!\n\nPut in at Johnson's Mill Rd. and take out on Hwy 501. If you park at the takeout on the river right, upstream side of the bridge, DO NOT park in the grass, keep all 4 tires on the pavement. The land owner has complained about this.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"5.1","correlations":[{"reachID":"1094","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"levelFT","belowRecommendedRangeComment":"Lots of Rock Dodging","lowRunnableRangeComment":"Not Scraping, current very mild","mediumRunnableRangeComment":"Current Picks up, not crazy yet","highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":"ItoIII","highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":"IItoIIIplus","beginLowRunnable":"2.5","beginMediumRunnable":"3.5","beginHighRunnable":"5","endHighRunnable":"10"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"LITTLE RIVER AT SR1461 NEAR ORANGE FACTORY, NC","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"0208521324","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"4","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"0.5","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"36.14166667","longitude":"-78.9191667"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/0208521324","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/0208521324/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"0.5","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"levelFT","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["109404","114647","FfsWlXGNwwghOMNqrynys","R0vW9ly2ueV95cEF4TxyR"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-78.949189,36.1638